All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed across the three modules:

**`src/auth.py`:**
- `has_permission`: made role comparison case-insensitive (`.lower()` on both sides)
- `is_admin_or_owner`: changed `and` to `or` — admin *or* owner should grant access, not both required

**`src/inventory.py`:**
- `__init__`: replaced mutable default `{}` with `None` default + `dict(initial)` copy, so two instances don't share the same dict
- `add`: changed from overwriting (`self._stock[sku] = qty`) to accumulating (`self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`)
- `reserve`: changed `>=` to `>` so reserving exactly the available quantity is allowed
- `release`: added validation that `qty` doesn't exceed reserved amount, raising `ValueError` instead of going negative

**`src/text_utils.py`:**
- `slugify`: lowercased alphanumeric characters (`.lower()`), and used `re.sub(r"-+", ...)` to collapse all repeated dashes (a single `.replace("--", "-")` only collapses one pair)
- `truncate`: slice now accounts for suffix length: `text[:max_len - len(suffix)]` so total length stays within `max_len`
